module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.DerivedPushforward.DirectSums
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.RightAdjointPushforward.PullbackComparisonStructureSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.Devissage.CompactGeneratedNatTrans

/-!
# Equation 48.8.0.1 is an isomorphism for every object of `D_QCoh`, given its inputs

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes and let `a` be a right adjoint of the restricted derived
direct image `Rf_* : D_QCoh(𝒪_X) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`. For `K, L ∈ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` the comparison map

  `Lf^*K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} a(L) ⟶ a(K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Y} L)`

of `Stacks.Duality.compareWithPullbackTensor`, the two-variable form of Equation 48.8.0.1 of
[Stacks, Tag 0A9S], is an isomorphism for *every* `K` as soon as it is one at a compact
generating family and both of its sides are exact and commute with direct sums. This is the
dévissage in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U], for an arbitrary morphism `f` and right adjoint
`a`, with its inputs as hypotheses. The lemma itself, for a perfect proper morphism of Noetherian
schemes and with no hypotheses beyond the source's, is
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullback_twistedInverseImage` (in
`PullbackComparisonUnconditional.lean`) and
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_twistedInverseImageCompareWithPullback_of_perfect_of_isProper` (in
`PullbackComparisonPerfectProper.lean`).

## The argument

The source's proof is a dévissage. Read in `K`, the comparison map is a morphism of functors

  `Lf^*(-) ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} a(L) ⟶ a((-) ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Y} L)`,

both of which are exact and commute with direct sums — on the right because `a` does, which is
[Stacks, Tag 0A9R], and because tensoring does. So the objects at which it is invertible form a
strictly full, saturated, triangulated subcategory stable under direct sums; since `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`
is generated by a single perfect object, which is [Stacks, Tag 09IS], the subcategory is
everything as soon as it contains that generator, and it does by [Stacks, Tag 0A9T], the perfect
case.

The dévissage itself is not redone here: it is
`StacksDraft.CompactDevissage.isIso_app_of_isCompactlyGenerated`, which takes a morphism of exact
direct-sum-preserving functors invertible on a compact generating family and concludes that it is
invertible everywhere, along the cell presentation of [Stacks, Tag 09SN]. All this file does is
exhibit the comparison map as such a morphism of functors — which is
`Stacks.Duality.compareWithPullbackTensor_naturality_left`, nothing more — and feed it in.

## Main definitions

All in the namespace `Stacks.Duality`.

* `quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight` — the endofunctor `K ↦ K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Z} L` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_Z)`,
  tensoring with `L` in the *first* variable.
* `quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight` — the functor `K ↦ Lf^*K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} M` from
  `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` to `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`, which at `M = a(L)` is the source of the comparison map.
* `compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans` — the comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A9S] read as a
  morphism of functors of `K`.

## Main results

* `isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isIso_generators` — the dévissage of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U]:
  the two-variable comparison map is an isomorphism for every `K ∈ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` once it is one at
  a compact generating family.
* `isIso_compareWithPullback_of_isIso_generators` — the same for the map displayed in
  [Stacks, Tag 0A9S], `Lf^*K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} a(𝒪_Y) ⟶ a(K)`.
* `isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isPerfect_generator` and
  `isIso_compareWithPullback_of_isPerfect_generator` — the two above with the invertibility at the
  generators replaced by the perfect case in the shape [Stacks, Tag 0A9T] states it, which is what
  a consumer has: the generating object of [Stacks, Tag 09IS] is perfect.

None of these carries a `@[stacks]` attribute: they state the dévissage over its inputs, and
[Stacks, Tag 0A9U] is registered at the two complete statements named above.

## The hypotheses

The inputs of the source's proof, which the complete statements of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U] discharge.

* **The perfect case, [Stacks, Tag 0A9T]**: the hypothesis `hgen`, asked for only at the members
  of the generating family. It is proved by
  `Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_and_compareWithPullback_of_isPerfect` of
  `PullbackComparisonPerfectDual.lean`.
* **Compact generation of `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`, [Stacks, Tag 09IS]**: the family `E` with `hEc` and
  `hE`. It is proved for quasi-compact quasi-separated `Y` by
  `Stacks.Duality.QcqsGeneration.isCompactlyGenerated_quasiCoherentDerivedCategory`.
* **The commutation of `a` with direct sums, [Stacks, Tag 0A9R]**: the instance binder
  `PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y L ⋙ a)`, together
  with the commutation of derived pullback and of the derived tensor product with direct sums on
  the other side. For a perfect proper morphism of Noetherian schemes it is
  `Stacks.Duality.preservesCoproducts_twistedInverseImage_of_perfect_proper`.
* **Exactness and compatibility with the shift** of the two sides and of the comparison map, which
  is what "strictly full, saturated, triangulated subcategory" asks for: the instance binders
  `Functor.CommShift`, `Functor.IsTriangulated` and
  `CategoryTheory.NatTrans.CommShift (compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans …) ℤ`.
* **The projection formula, [Stacks, Tag 08EU]**, and the oplax monoidality `α` of derived
  pullback, inherited unchanged from `Stacks.Duality.compareWithPullbackTensor`.

*The model of the derived categories.* As in `PullbackComparison.lean`, no declaration here
carries a `[HasDerivedCategory.{w}]` binder: the quasi-coherent derived tensor product and derived
pullback are available only at the locally small model
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory`, whose morphisms live in `Type u`. That is
also the universe at which `D_QCoh` has direct sums
(`Stacks.Duality.DerivedPushforward.hasCoproducts_quasiCoherentDerivedCategory`) and the universe
at which the cell presentation tests compactness, so `ι : Type u` and `IsCompactObject.{u}` below
are forced rather than chosen.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9S)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09SN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09SN)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
open Stacks.Duality.DerivedPushforward

universe u

namespace Stacks.Duality

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Y)
  (hpush : ∀ (K : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X) (i : ℤ),
    ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor Y.Modules i).obj
      ((derivedPushforward f).obj K.obj)).IsQuasicoherent)
  (α : quasiCoherentDerivedTensorSwap Y ⋙ quasiCoherentDerivedPullback' f ⟶
      (quasiCoherentDerivedPullback' f).prod (quasiCoherentDerivedPullback' f) ⋙
        quasiCoherentDerivedTensorSwap X)

/-! ### The two sides of the comparison map as functors of `K` -/

/-- Tensoring with `L` in the first variable: the endofunctor `K ↦ K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Z} L` of
`D_QCoh(𝒪_Z)`. This is the shape in which the right unitor `ρ` of
`Stacks.Duality.compareWithPullback` is already stated. -/
abbrev quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight (Z : Scheme.{u}) (L : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Z) :
    quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Z ⥤ quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Z :=
  (quasiCoherentDerivedTensor Z).flip.obj L

/-- Derived pullback followed by tensoring with `M` in the first variable: the functor
`K ↦ Lf^*K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} M` from `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` to `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`. At `M = a(L)` it is the source of
the two-variable comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A9S], read as a functor of `K`. -/
abbrev quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight (M : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X) :
    quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y ⥤ quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X :=
  quasiCoherentDerivedPullback' f ⋙ quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight X M

section Comparison

variable [∀ (E : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X) (K : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y),
    IsIso (projectionFormulaMap f hpush α E K)]
  {a : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y ⥤ quasiCoherentDerivedCategory X}
  (adj : quasiCoherentDerivedPushforward f hpush ⊣ a)

/-- **The comparison map of Equation 48.8.0.1 as a morphism of functors of `K`.** The maps
`Lf^*K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} a(L) ⟶ a(K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Y} L)` of `Stacks.Duality.compareWithPullbackTensor`, for a
fixed `L`, assembled into a morphism

  `Lf^*(-) ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} a(L) ⟶ a((-) ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Y} L)`

of functors `D_QCoh(𝒪_Y) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`. Naturality is
`Stacks.Duality.compareWithPullbackTensor_naturality_left`. -/
def compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans (L : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) :
    quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f (a.obj L) ⟶
      quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y L ⋙ a where
  app K := compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj K L
  naturality _ _ h := compareWithPullbackTensor_naturality_left f hpush α adj h L

/-- The morphism of functors has the comparison maps as its components. -/
@[simp]
theorem compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans_app (K L : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) :
    (compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans f hpush α adj L).app K =
      compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj K L :=
  rfl

/-! ### The dévissage -/

section Devissage

variable (L : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y)
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f (a.obj L)).CommShift ℤ]
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y L ⋙ a).CommShift ℤ]
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f (a.obj L)).IsTriangulated]
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y L ⋙ a).IsTriangulated]
  [∀ J : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
    (quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f (a.obj L))]
  [∀ J : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
    (quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y L ⋙ a)]
  [NatTrans.CommShift (compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans f hpush α adj L) ℤ]

/-- **The dévissage of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U].** Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a morphism of schemes, let `a` be
a right adjoint of `Rf_* : D_QCoh(𝒪_X) ⥤ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`, and let `L ∈ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`. Suppose
`D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)` is generated by a family `E` of compact objects, suppose both sides of the
two-variable comparison map of [Stacks, Tag 0A9S] are exact and commute with direct sums as
functors of `K`, suppose the comparison map commutes with the shift, and suppose it is invertible
at each `E i`. Then it is invertible at *every* `K ∈ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`.

This is the argument of the source's Lemma 48.13.3, whose complete statement is
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullback_twistedInverseImage`. The hypothesis `hgen` is
[Stacks, Tag 0A9T], the perfect case, asked for only at the generators; `E`, `hEc` and `hE` are
the compact generation of [Stacks, Tag 09IS]; the direct-sum preservation of
`quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y L ⋙ a` is [Stacks, Tag 0A9R], that `a` commutes with direct
sums. The dévissage is `StacksDraft.CompactDevissage.isIso_app_of_isCompactlyGenerated`. -/
theorem isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isIso_generators {ι : Type u}
    (E : ι → quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) (hEc : ∀ i, IsCompactObject.{u} (E i))
    (hE : ∀ Z : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y,
      ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Z → IsZero Z)
    (hgen : ∀ i, IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj (E i) L))
    (K : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) :
    IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj K L) :=
  StacksDraft.CompactDevissage.isIso_app_of_isCompactlyGenerated
    (compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans f hpush α adj L) E hEc hE hgen K

/-- **The dévissage of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U], with the perfect case in the shape [Stacks, Tag 0A9T]
states it.** The same conclusion as
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isIso_generators`, with the invertibility at
the generators replaced by the hypothesis `hperf` that the comparison map is invertible at every
*perfect* object, together with `hEperf`, the perfectness of the generating family. This is what
a consumer has: the generator produced by [Stacks, Tag 09IS] is perfect, and `hperf` is the
conclusion of `Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_and_compareWithPullback_of_isPerfect`,
which is [Stacks, Tag 0A9T].

No `@[stacks]` attribute: this is a repackaging of the hypotheses of the dévissage above, not
content of its own; 0A9T and 0A9U are registered where they are proved. -/
theorem isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isPerfect_generator {ι : Type u}
    (E : ι → quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) (hEc : ∀ i, IsCompactObject.{u} (E i))
    (hE : ∀ Z : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y,
      ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Z → IsZero Z)
    (hEperf : ∀ i, Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect
      (X := Y.toRingedSpace) (E i).obj)
    (hperf : ∀ P : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y,
      Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace) P.obj →
      IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj P L))
    (K : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) :
    IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj K L) :=
  isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isIso_generators f hpush α adj L E hEc hE
    (fun i => hperf (E i) (hEperf i)) K

end Devissage

/-! ### The map displayed in Equation 48.8.0.1 -/

section StructureSheaf

variable (ρ : (quasiCoherentDerivedTensor Y).flip.obj (derivedStructureSheaf Y) ≅ 𝟭 _)
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f
    (a.obj (derivedStructureSheaf Y))).CommShift ℤ]
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y (derivedStructureSheaf Y) ⋙ a).CommShift ℤ]
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f
    (a.obj (derivedStructureSheaf Y))).IsTriangulated]
  [(quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y (derivedStructureSheaf Y) ⋙ a).IsTriangulated]
  [∀ J : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
    (quasiCoherentDerivedPullbackTensorRight f (a.obj (derivedStructureSheaf Y)))]
  [∀ J : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
    (quasiCoherentDerivedTensorRight Y (derivedStructureSheaf Y) ⋙ a)]
  [NatTrans.CommShift
    (compareWithPullbackTensorNatTrans f hpush α adj (derivedStructureSheaf Y)) ℤ]

/-- **The dévissage of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U], for the map the source displays.** Equation 48.8.0.1 of
[Stacks, Tag 0A9S], the map `Lf^*K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_X} a(𝒪_Y) ⟶ a(K)`, is an isomorphism for every
`K ∈ D_QCoh(𝒪_Y)`: it is the two-variable comparison map at `L = 𝒪_Y`, which is an isomorphism by
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isIso_generators`, followed by `a` applied to
the right unitor `K ⊗ᴸ_{𝒪_Y} 𝒪_Y ≅ K`. -/
theorem isIso_compareWithPullback_of_isIso_generators {ι : Type u}
    (E : ι → quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) (hEc : ∀ i, IsCompactObject.{u} (E i))
    (hE : ∀ Z : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y,
      ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Z → IsZero Z)
    (hgen : ∀ i, IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj (E i)
      (derivedStructureSheaf Y)))
    (K : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) :
    IsIso (compareWithPullback f hpush α adj ρ K) := by
  have h₁ : IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj K (derivedStructureSheaf Y)) :=
    isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isIso_generators f hpush α adj
      (derivedStructureSheaf Y) E hEc hE hgen K
  have h₂ : IsIso (ρ.hom.app K) := NatIso.isIso_app_of_isIso ρ.hom K
  have h₃ : IsIso (a.map (ρ.hom.app K)) := a.map_isIso _
  change IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj K (derivedStructureSheaf Y) ≫
    a.map (ρ.hom.app K))
  infer_instance

/-- **The dévissage of [Stacks, Tag 0A9U] for the displayed map, with the perfect case in the shape
[Stacks, Tag 0A9T] states it.** As
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullback_of_isIso_generators`, with the invertibility at the
generators replaced by `hperf`, invertibility at every perfect object, and `hEperf`, perfectness
of the generating family. No `@[stacks]` attribute, for the reason given at
`Stacks.Duality.isIso_compareWithPullbackTensor_of_isPerfect_generator`. -/
theorem isIso_compareWithPullback_of_isPerfect_generator {ι : Type u}
    (E : ι → quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) (hEc : ∀ i, IsCompactObject.{u} (E i))
    (hE : ∀ Z : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y,
      ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Z → IsZero Z)
    (hEperf : ∀ i, Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect
      (X := Y.toRingedSpace) (E i).obj)
    (hperf : ∀ P : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y,
      Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes.IsPerfect (X := Y.toRingedSpace) P.obj →
      IsIso (compareWithPullbackTensor f hpush α adj P (derivedStructureSheaf Y)))
    (K : quasiCoherentDerivedCategory Y) :
    IsIso (compareWithPullback f hpush α adj ρ K) :=
  isIso_compareWithPullback_of_isIso_generators f hpush α adj ρ E hEc hE
    (fun i => hperf (E i) (hEperf i)) K

end StructureSheaf

end Comparison

end Stacks.Duality

end
